"hadiths[36]{hadithnumber,text}:"
127201,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that A'isha
127202,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that A'isha
127301,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha
127302,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha
127401,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that A'isha umm al-muminin told him that Aflah
127402,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that A'isha umm al-muminin told him that Aflah
127501,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about animals slaughtered by the Christian Arabs. He said, ""There is no harm in them,"" but he recited this ayat, ""Whoever takes them as friends is from them."" (Sura 5 ayat)"
127502,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about animals slaughtered by the Christian Arabs. He said, ""There is no harm in them,"" but he recited this ayat, ""Whoever takes them as friends is from them."" (Sura 5 ayat)"
127601,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Amr ibn ash- Sharid that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked whether
127602,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Amr ibn ash- Sharid that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked whether
127701,"Yahya related to me from Malik thal Yahya ibn Said heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Sulayman ibn Yasar both mention that Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As divorced the daughter of Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Hakam irrevocably, so Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Hakam took her away A'isha umm al-muminin sent to Marwan ibn al-Hakam who was the Amir of al-Madina at that time. She said, ""Fear Allah and make him return the woman to her house."" Marwan said in what Sulayman related, ''Abd ar-Rahman has the upper hand over me."" Marwan said in what al-Qasim related, ""Hasn't the affair of Fatima bint Qays reached you?"" A'isha said, ""You are forced to mention the story of Fatima "" Marwan said, ""If you know that evil, whatever evil there was between those two is enough for you."" Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Try to go straight, although you will not be able to do so. Act, and the best of your actions is the prayer. And only a mumin is constant in his wudu."".)"""""
127702,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, made zakat al-fitr obligatory, a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley, on every Muslim, young and old, male and female, free and slave."" Abdullah ibn Umar added, ""The people made an equivalent to two mudd of wheat."""
127801,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that A'isha umm al-muminin sent him away while he was being nursed to her sister Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr as-Siddiq and said, ""Suckle him ten times so that he can come in to see me."" Salim said, ""Umm Kulthum nursed me three times and then fell ill, so that she only nursed me three times. I could not go in to see A'isha because Umm Kulthum did not finish for me the ten times"
127802,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that A'isha umm al-muminin sent him away while he was being nursed to her sister Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr as-Siddiq and said, ""Suckle him ten times so that he can come in to see me."" Salim said, ""Umm Kulthum nursed me three times and then fell ill, so that she only nursed me three times. I could not go in to see A'isha because Umm Kulthum did not finish for me the ten times"
127901,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd told him that Hafsa
127902,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd told him that Hafsa
128001,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father told him that A'isha
128002,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father told him that A'isha
128101,"This hadith is cut off. Here is the complete version:

Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibrahim ibn Uqba asked Said ibn al-Musayyab about suckling. Said said, ""All that occurs in the first two years, even if it is only a drop, makes haram. Whatever is after two years, is only food that is eaten."" Ibrahim ibn Uqba said, ""Then I asked Urwa ibn az-Zubayr and he told me the same as what Said ibn al-Musayyab said."""
128102,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibrahim ibn Uqba asked Said ibn al-Musayyab about suckling. Said said, ""All that occurs in the first two years, even if it is only a drop, makes haram. Whatever is after two years, is only food that is eaten."" Ibrahim ibn Uqba said, ''Then I asked Urwa ibn az-Zubayr and he told me the same as what Said ibn al-Musayyab said."""
128201,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say
128202,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say
128301,"**Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that he said, ""The blood-money for a Jew or a Christian is half the blood-money for a free Muslim.""**"
128302,"Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: Barirah came and said: ""I have contracted my manumission with my people for nine uqiyah, one uqiyah each year. So help me."" Aisha said: ""If your people like that I count it out for them from you all at once, and the wala' (right of patronage) be for me, I will do so."" Barirah went to her people and said that to them. They refused her, except that the wala' be for them. She came back from her people while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting. She said to Aisha: ""I presented that to them and they refused me, except that the wala' be for them."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard that, so he asked her. Aisha informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Buy her and stipulate the wala' for them, for the wala' belongs only to the one who frees."" So Aisha did that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""As for what follows: What is the matter with men who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Any condition not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it be a hundred conditions. The judgment of Allah is more right, and the condition of Allah is more binding. The wala' belongs only to the one who frees."""""""
128401,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that he was asked about the suckling of an older person. He said, ''Urwa ibn az-Zubayr informed me that Abu Hudhayfa ibn Utba ibn Rabia, one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who was present at Badr, adopted Salim (who is called Salim, the mawla of Abu Hudhayfa) as the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, adopted Zayd ibn Haritha. He thought of him as his son, and Abu Hudhayfa married him to his brother's sister, Fatima bint al-Walid ibn Utba ibn Rabia, who was at that time among the first emigrants. She was one of the best unmarried women of the Quraysh. When Allah the Exalted sent down in His Book what He sent down about Zayd ibn Haritha, 'Call them after their true fathers. That is more equitable in the sight of Allah. If you do not know who their fathers were then they are your brothers in the deen and your mawali,' (Sura 33 ayat 5) people in this position were traced back to their fathers. When the father was not known, they were traced to their mawla. ""Sahla bint Suhayl who was the wife of Abu Hudhayfa, and one of the tribe of Amr ibn Luayy, came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, 'Messenger of Allah! We think of Salim as a son and he comes in to see me while I am uncovered. We only have one room, so what do you think about the situation?' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Give him five drinks of your milk and he will be mahram by it.' She then saw him as a foster son. A'isha umm al-muminin took that as a precedent for whatever men she wanted to be able to come to see her. She ordered her sister, Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr as-Siddiq and the daughters of her brother to give milk to whichever men she wanted to be able to come in to see her. The rest of the wives of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, refused to let anyone come in to them by such nursing. They said, 'No! By Allah! We think that what the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ordered Sahla bint Suhayl to do was only an indulgence concerning the nursing of Salim alone. No! By Allah! No one will come in upon us by such nursing!' ""This is what the wives of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, thought about the suckling of an older person"
128402,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that he was asked about the suckling of an older person. He said, ''Urwa ibn az-Zubayr informed me that Abu Hudhayfa ibn Utba ibn Rabia, one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who was present at Badr, adopted Salim (who is called Salim, the mawla of Abu Hudhayfa) as the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, adopted Zayd ibn Haritha. He thought of him as his son, and Abu Hudhayfa married him to his brother's sister, Fatima bint al-Walid ibn Utba ibn Rabia, who was at that time among the first emigrants. She was one of the best unmarried women of the Quraysh. When Allah the Exalted sent down in His Book what He sent down about Zayd ibn Haritha, 'Call them after their true fathers. That is more equitable in the sight of Allah. If you do not know who their fathers were then they are your brothers in the deen and your mawali,' (Sura 33 ayat 5) people in this position were traced back to their fathers. When the father was not known, they were traced to their mawla. ""Sahla bint Suhayl who was the wife of Abu Hudhayfa, and one of the tribe of Amr ibn Luayy, came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, 'Messenger of Allah! We think of Salim as a son and he comes in to see me while I am uncovered. We only have one room, so what do you think about the situation?' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Give him five drinks of your milk and he will be mahram by it.' She then saw him as a foster son. A'isha umm al-muminin took that as a precedent for whatever men she wanted to be able to come to see her. She ordered her sister, Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr as-Siddiq and the daughters of her brother to give milk to whichever men she wanted to be able to come in to see her. The rest of the wives of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, refused to let anyone come in to them by such nursing. They said, 'No! By Allah! We think that what the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ordered Sahla bint Suhayl to do was only an indulgence concerning the nursing of Salim alone. No! By Allah! No one will come in upon us by such nursing!' ""This is what the wives of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, thought about the suckling of an older person"
128501,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Dinar said, ""I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say, 'The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade the selling of fruits until their good condition became evident.'"""
128502,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said, ""Divorce belongs to men, and women have the idda."""""""
128601,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that a man said to Abu Musa al-Ashari
128602,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that a man said to Abu Musa al-Ashari
128701,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Sulayman ibn Yasar and from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from A'isha umm al- muminin
128702,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Sulayman ibn Yasar and from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from A'isha umm al- muminin
128801,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Nawfal said that A'isha, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to say, ""When any of you does the ritual prayer for rain, let him turn his cloak inside out."""
128802,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Nawfal said that he asked A'isha, umm al-muminin, about a man kissing his wife when he was fasting. A'isha said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss when he was fasting, so do not overburden yourselves."""
128901,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that A'isha
128902,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that A'isha
